lexopt (the Meadow package) is a port of the Rust crate lexopt
(https://github.com/blyxxyz/lexopt), version 0.3.2, by Jan Verbeek and
contributors, to Meadow. Its test cases are generated from that crate, and its
code is translated from the crate's source. The crate is licensed under the
MIT license, and so is this port: see LICENSE.

src/Tables.mw lists the characters Rust's standard library escapes when it
formats a string with `{:?}`, generated by running that library. The Rust
standard library is by the Rust project contributors and is dual-licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0, and the MIT license
(https://github.com/rust-lang/rust); the table is used here under the MIT
license.
